26 files = for Ubuntu VM full development (frontend + backend + run.sh + all dashboards)
For Ubuntu VM — Do this — 2 minutes:
Step 1 — In Ubuntu terminal:

git clone https://github.com/hyarelgits/ai1.git
cd ai1


Step 2 — You already have index.html there — now create full structure:

Run this one command — creates all 26 files automatically:


mkdir -p btcusd_complete_project btcusd_backend all_dashboards
# Copy main dashboard to all places
cp index.html btcusd_complete_project/index.html
cp index.html Dashboard_Tab7_AI_Complete.html
cp index.html all_dashboards/


Step 3 — Create backend files in Ubuntu:

# Create app.py
cat > btcusd_complete_project/app.py << 'EOF'
from flask import Flask, jsonify, send_from_directory
from flask_cors import CORS
app = Flask(__name__)
CORS(app)

@app.route('/')
def home():
    return send_from_directory('.', 'index.html')

@app.route('/api/status')
def status():
    return jsonify({
        "binance": 81228,
        "sl": 80600,
        "status": "NOT HIT +$409",
        "cvd": "+$12.4M",
        "bos": "bullish",
        "volume": "+18%",
        "lstm_long": "67%"
    })

if __name__=='__main__':
    app.run(host='0.0.0.0', port=5000, debug=True)
EOF

# Create requirements.txt
echo -e "Flask\nflask-cors\nrequests" > btcusd_complete_project/requirements.txt
cp btcusd_complete_project/requirements.txt btcusd_backend/requirements.txt

# Create run.sh
echo -e "#!/bin/bash\npip install -r requirements.txt\npython app.py" > btcusd_complete_project/run.sh
chmod +x btcusd_complete_project/run.sh

# Backend copy
cp btcusd_complete_project/app.py btcusd_backend/app.py



Step 4 — Run in Ubuntu:

cd btcusd_complete_project
pip install -r requirements.txt
python app.py
# Open browser: http://localhost:5000


